    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0608" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112A European War 1939/29899:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Bolwia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Boal</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-07T12:00:00-04:00">May 7, 1943—noon.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>658. Your 833, May 1, 2 p.m. The Bolivian Foreign Minister<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d538-f1"/> has informed the Department that he has telegraphed to La
                    Paz, urging the issuance of a supplementary decree extending functions of
                    Economic Defense Board of Bolivia to cover implementation of supreme decrees of
                    December 11 and 12, 1941. As soon as such a decree is promulgated, please
                    telegraph text to the Department urgently with your comments as to whether it
                    meets satisfactorily the second objection raised by Ramsey to the decree of
                    April 30, 1943.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d538-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d538-f1" n="40" xml:id="d538-f1-content">
                <p>Foreign Minister Elio accompanied President Peñaranda on his visit to
                    Washington.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d538-f2" n="41" xml:id="d538-f2-content">
                <p>For text, see telegram No. 832, May 1, from the Chargé in Bolivia, <ref
                        target="#pg594">p. 594</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
